  global g_deviceId — a second openDevice orphans the first.
* (LOW, bug hunt 1.1.70) `crate replicate` can wedge itself: zfs recv
  runs without -F (replicate_pure.cpp:188-192), and replicate.cpp:
  129-137 destroys the local snapshot on ANY pipeline error even when
  the remote already received it — the remote then holds a newer
  snapshot and every later incremental is refused. An ssh failure reads
  as "no common snapshot" (replicate.cpp:84-91) and the full send that
  follows fails too. (pickLatestCommonSuffix itself is right.) Tell
  "dataset does not exist" from other errors; check the remote before
  destroying.
* (LOW, bug hunt 1.1.70) a signal death loses its signal in the exit
  code: `returnCode = WIFEXITED ? WEXITSTATUS : 1` (run.cpp:2428, 2494)
  — 1 instead of 128+N (the reason text keeps it, run_jail.cpp:423).
  And exit code 124 means both "timed out" and "user switch failed" in
  JailExec (jail_query.cpp:458,461; privops_handlers.cpp:865), or a
  program's own `exit 124`, when run/timeout is set.
* (LOW, bug hunt 1.1.70, latent) wrap's .desktop Exec quoting
  (wrap_pure.cpp:17-32) puts three backslashes before `"`, `` ` ``, `$`
  where the Desktop Entry spec wants two, and does not double '%'.
  Unreachable today: the path is CRATE_PATH_CRATE and the names are
  [A-Za-z0-9._-] (args_pure.cpp:323-337, profile_pure.cpp:10-24).
* (LOW, bug hunt 1.1.70, latent) StatusPure::LineBuffer: the newline
  that ends an overlong line runs buf_.clear() (status_pure.cpp:198),
  wiping complete lines still queued before it (feed("A\n" + 70000 x
  + "\nB\n") yields only B). waitForJail takes lines after every 4096-
  byte read (status_fd.cpp:116), so it does not happen there.
* (LOW, bug hunt 1.1.70) JsonPure::escape passes bytes >= 0x80 through
  (json_pure.cpp:27, documented json_pure.h:20-21): invalid UTF-8 in an
  error text, a command or a path reaches the --status-fd stream
  (status_pure.cpp:23-27) and crated / hub responses, which strict
  readers (Python json.loads on bytes) refuse. Replace invalid
  sequences with \ufffd.
* (MED, left open by 1.1.75) host-side writes into a jail tree still run
  as root by path while the tree may hold jail-made symlinks: on a
  --warm-base clone (the source jail's root wrote it) writeFileInJail /
  appendFileInJail (/etc/rc.conf, /etc/hostid, /var/cron/tabs/<user>,
  the init marker; run.cpp) go through Util::Fs::writeFile / appendFile,
  whose O_NOFOLLOW guards the last component only: a symlinked directory
  — /etc -> /etc, absolute, resolves against the HOST's root — sends the
  append to the host's /etc/rc.conf. Write through an openat() walk that
  refuses symlinked components (O_RESOLVE_BENEATH), or inside the jail.
* (LOW, left open by 1.1.75) the trusted spec store of warm templates
  (/var/db/crate/warm/<guid>.spec / .thin) is never pruned: a destroyed
  template leaves its files (harmless — a new dataset gets a new guid).
  `crate clean` could drop entries whose guid no dataset has. `crate
  info` / `list` of a running warm-base jail still show the clone's own
  +CRATE.SPEC, not the trusted one it runs with.
* (MED, bug hunt 1.1.71) 1.1.71's X-cookie move follows a symlink in the
  SOURCE (run.cpp:2411-2429): it runs for every root `crate run` with
  the default run user, X11 or not, and fileExists / copy_file of
  J("/root/.Xauthority") follow a link that the jail's root (rc,
  services, a saved rootfs) placed there — `/root/.Xauthority ->
  /etc/master.passwd` copies the HOST file into /home/crate/.Xauthority,
  owned by the run user. chown and chmod after the copy follow links
  too. Fix: lstat + S_ISREG, open O_NOFOLLOW, copy by fd, fchown/fchmod.
* (MED, bug hunt 1.1.71) JailQuery::findContainer ignores the owner and
  the kind of jail (jail_query.cpp:263-288). Root `crate stop web`, HTTP
  DELETE or restart hit another tenant's web_pidN when the own `web` is
  not running (before: not found); start answers 409 when ANY tenant
  runs that name (profiles: `firefox`); start by kernel name web_pid1
  misses a running web_pid999; a non-crate jail (a bastille `web`) is
  stopped, updated or restarted; container `3` is shadowed by jid 3.
  Fix: prefer the registry owner's jail, crate jails only,
  containerNameOf(name) for start.
* (MED, bug hunt 1.1.71) warm-base teardown leaks the clone when it has
  snapshots (run.cpp:503-510, zfs_ops.cpp:102-117: destroy without -r) —
  after any backup, replicate, snapshot create or template warm of it.
  The clone stays mounted, @warmrun pinned, and a later clean empties
  it.
* (MED, bug hunt 1.1.71) `cow:` and `base_container:` do nothing
  (run.cpp:717-768, 787-813): the ZFS clone is made but the jail does
  not use it, `persistent` leaves a clone and a snapshot of the parent
  on every run, and the unionfs …-cow-writable directory is neither
  reused nor removed. Documented in crate.5:692-705, 1139-1153.
* (MED, bug hunt 1.1.71) dns_filter writes unbound.conf and points
  resolv.conf at 127.0.0.1 but never installs or starts unbound
  (run_services.cpp:25-61): chromium-privacy.yml and
  templates/privacy.yml have no DNS; dns_filter/allow is parsed and
  unused; with unbound present the mkdir at :59 hits EEXIST (plausible).
  Fix: unbound into pkg and services in preprocess, allow as local-zone
  transparent.
* (MED, bug hunt 1.1.71) signals: there is no SIGHUP handler
  (run.cpp:377-386), so a dropped ssh session kills `crate run` without
  any RunAtEnd — jail (persist), shares, epair, rules, leases and clones
  stay. On the root path SIGTERM is not forwarded to the child and
  waitpid is retried on EINTR (jail_query.cpp:488-490), so `kill <pid>`
  waits for the command; the comment at run.cpp:397 says otherwise.
* (MED, bug hunt 1.1.71) the healthcheck runs as two users: the start-up
  waitForHealthy as the operator (run.cpp:2386; root for a root
  operator), the background monitor as runUser (run.cpp:2518; `crate`).
  A check that needs root passes at start and fails in the monitor;
  retries are counted differently (retries+1 attempts vs >= retries);
  crate.5:1083 says "as root", impossible under rootless.
* (MED, bug hunt 1.1.71) the root-path JailExec hands the whole crate(1)
  environment to the jail (jail_query.cpp:461-482): secrets in the
  operator's environment reach the jail; crated builds a minimal one
  (privops_handlers.cpp:1012-1021).
* (MED, bug hunt 1.1.71) `crate throttle` cannot apply anything: it
  needs jail->ip4 (throttle.cpp:143), and crate's networked jails are
  always vnet (run_jail.cpp:159), where ip4.addr is empty.
* (MED, bug hunt 1.1.71) `crate logs` shows no console log:
  /var/log/crate/<name>/{console,stdout}.log are written by nothing (no
  writer in lib/ or daemon/; GET /logs looks for them too). It falls
  back to the jail's /var/log/messages read FROM THE HOST, following a
  jail-planted symlink (a host file is printed) or hanging on a FIFO
  (lifecycle.cpp:279-298).
* (MED, bug hunt 1.1.71) console.cpp:40-54 and info.cpp:46-62 keep a
  fallback that matches "jail-"+target as a prefix, via stoi(), and by
  hostname — by default the host's own for every jail — and bypasses
  findContainer's ambiguity refusal: `crate console web` with web
  stopped and webapp running opens a root login in webapp.
* (MED, bug hunt 1.1.71) `crate gui`: the registry stores web_pid4242
  and the jail- prefix never matches (gui_registry.cpp:91-111), so the
  example at args.cpp:277-283, `crate gui focus firefox`, fails; a jid
  is taken for a display number or a pid.
* (MED, bug hunt 1.1.71) `crate import` copies with copy_file through a
  dangling symlink at the derived output (/tmp/x.txz -> /tmp/x.crate),
  and chown follows it too (import.cpp:272, util.cpp:864) — the import
  variant of 1.1.71's export fix.
* (LOW, bug hunt 1.1.71) a jail leaks on an ERR between run.cpp:1165 and
  :1274 (acquire_fw_lease 409/503), and rmdirHier then removes the root
  of the live jail — reachable once §1's privops blockers are fixed.
  backup-prune exits 0 when an unlink failed (backup_prune.cpp:131-139).
  The `snapshot list` fallback uses -r (zfs_ops.cpp:321-326); 1.1.69's
  -d 1 did not reach it. export.cpp:44-57's fallback bypasses the
  ambiguity refusal, and its default file name comes from the hostname,
  which a jail with allow_set_hostname controls (may contain '/').
  `crate console web ls /tmp` joins the words into one argv element
  (args.cpp:1241-1247 -> console.cpp:89, execvp("ls /tmp")), and the
  command's own options (-l) are taken for crate's. chown/chmod by path
  after services started (run.cpp:2422-2423, 2500-2503) race with a
