  qualify, and the first template needs a jail on its own dataset. Make
  `crate run` create <dataset of /var/run/crate>/jail-<name>-<hex> when
  that directory is on ZFS.

=== 8. crate-hub ===

* (LOW) hub/store.cpp shares one sqlite3 handle between the poller
  thread and the HTTP threads with no mutex and no busy_timeout; it
  works because sqlite's default serialized threading mode locks per
  call. Add a Store mutex (or one connection per thread) before any
  multi-statement operation is added.

* (MED) Dashboard actions still go browser → crated directly with
  https:// hard-coded, and crated emits no CORS headers, so the
  cross-origin fetch is blocked. Route start/stop/restart/destroy
  through the hub (POST /api/v1/nodes/:node/containers/:name/<verb>
  with the hub holding per-node admin tokens — a trust-model change)
  or document the dashboard as read-only.

* (LOW) store.cpp: one sqlite3* shared by poller and HTTP threads
  with no mutex (safe only with SQLITE_THREADSAFE=1 — plausible).
  poller.cpp: a down node costs two 5 s timeouts so N down nodes can
  exceed poll_interval. api.cpp /api/v1/ha/orders emits failover
  orders from the hub's own view only (hub-side partition → orders
  while the primary is healthy; mitigated because `crate migrate`
  needs the source).
* (MED, bug hunt 1.1.71) the hub's sqlite store is write-only and grows
  without bound: recordPoll on every poll (poller.cpp:198), no SELECT
  anywhere, prune only through the POST endpoint (api.cpp:230-239; the
  comment at :227 says "called by main loop") — 5760 rows per node per
  day with full jls JSON; sqlite3_step results are unchecked
  (store.cpp:50,60).
* (MED, bug hunt 1.1.71, plausible) one slow node stalls the whole
  poller and can exhaust memory: the read timeout is per recv, there is
  no overall deadline, and the body is unbounded (poller.cpp:151-173). A
  node, or a MITM on a plain node, that dribbles a byte every <10 s
  holds the single poller thread: the other nodes' state freezes, a
  primary that dies meanwhile stays "reachable", pollerThread.join hangs
  (main.cpp:308). Variant of the 2x5 s item above.
* (MED, bug hunt 1.1.71, plausible) the dashboard shows the wrong names
  and no IPs: crated serves `jls --libxo json` without parameters
  (routes.cpp:180-182), whose default fields are jid, ipv4, hostname and
  path — no name; app.js:134-137 shows the hostname as Name (the host's
  own under privacy/hostname: host) and reads ip4/ip/IP, not ipv4.
* (LOW, bug hunt 1.1.71) the datacenter name is not JSON-escaped
  (datacenter_pure.cpp:59; validateName at :11 is never called;
  poller.cpp:71): a quote breaks the document, Promise.all (app.js:196)
  fails and the dashboard is empty, and a crafted name injects an object
  whose nodes_total app.js:110-113 renders unescaped (config-sourced).
  extractContainerArray counts [ and { together
  (aggregator_pure.cpp:79-90). crate-hub.8's example config holds admin
  tokens where viewer ones suffice (routes.cpp:1168,1192), and the
  config file's mode is never checked; the dashboard keeps one
  crate-admin-token for every node (app.js:37-41). /admin/prune's
  loopback check (api.cpp:231) is no origin check behind a reverse
  proxy; no set_payload_max_length. crate-hub.8: `schedule` runs `crate
  migrate` unless --dry-run, and SYNOPSIS lacks -b. `port:` is ignored
  when the host contains ':' (poller.cpp:65).

=== 9. crate-snmpd ===

* (MED) CRATE-MIB table and traps are not implemented but documented
  as the product: mib.cpp answers noSuchInstance for every non-scalar
  OID; resolveGetNext walks only 4 scalars; sendTrap only logs.
  snmpd/CRATE-MIB.txt:65-165 defines an 11-column table plus
  NOTIFICATION-TYPEs; README.md:761-763 says the agent "exposes
  container metrics". collector.h:20 says "CPU% x 100" but
  collector.cpp:52 stores raw percent; netRx/netTx/uptimeTicks never
  populated. Either implement the table + Notify PDUs or trim the MIB
  and README to the four scalars.
* (MED, bug hunt 1.1.71) CRATE-MIB.txt and the agent disagree: the MIB
  is enterprises 60117 with version .1.1, hostname .1.2, count .1.3,
  running .1.4 (CRATE-MIB.txt:24,33-59); the agent registers 59999 with
  count .1.1, running .1.2, version .1.3, hostname .1.4 (mib.cpp:70-76).
  CRATE-MIB::crateContainerRunning.0 from the man page resolves to an
  OID the agent does not serve. Separate from the table / traps item
  above.
* (MED, bug hunt 1.1.71) the running count is always 0:
  collector.cpp:26-35 compares jls' `dying` with "0", but jls prints
  booleans as false/true; without -d jls does not list dying jails
  anyway, and the count covers every host jail while the man page says
  crate jails. daemon/metrics.cpp:35-41 has the same parse, so
  crate_containers_running is always 0 too. Fix: false/true as in
  jail_query.cpp:126, crate jails only.
* (LOW, bug hunt 1.1.71) crate-snmpd.8 and mib.cpp:9 describe a bsnmpd
  setup, but base bsnmpd has no snmp_agentx.so — only net-snmp works
  (plausible for third-party ports); the man page's "collector thread"
  is the main loop (main.cpp:111-116), which blocks AgentX while it
  collects; main.cpp:5 promises the table and traps; registerMib's
  result is ignored (main.cpp:70,98), with no retry.
* (LOW, left open by 1.1.72) AgentX: 1.1.72 answers Get, GetNext
  (include bit, range end) and GetBulk, and refuses TestSet with
  notWritable; the container table and the traps are still the MED item
  above. Nothing exercises the agent against a real net-snmp master in
  CI.

